{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "1.&nbsp;The proposed development would result in the loss of two family-sized dwellinghouses, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need, and further would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers. Furthermore, the proposal would have indeqaute quality of acommodation which could pose harm to future residents. Additionally, the development site is not located within an area of high access to public transport and is therefore not considered an appropriate location for an HMO. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan&nbsp;(September 2024)East London HMO Guidance (4)",
    "The proposal lacks sufficient clarity regarding the internal layout and the number of intended occupants, particularly in relation to bedroom no.2, where the submitted drawings (dated 10/04/2025) do not accurately reflect measurable dimensions. This lack of clarity compromises the ability of the Local Planning Authority to properly assess the quality of accommodation proposed, and may prejudice third parties who would otherwise have had the opportunity to comment on the application. As such, the proposal fails to demonstrate compliance with the relevant requirements of the Development Plan. This is unacceptable and contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SP2 and&nbsp;DMD1 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
